e... but the description said 17 people.\n\nHmm, but the total is 135,000. Let me try: 9*10000 + 4*5000 + 1*15000 = 90000+20000+15000 = 125,000. That doesn't work.\n\n8*10000 + 5*5000 + 1*15000 = 80000+25000+15000 = 120,000. Doesn't work.\n\nLet me just look at what the OCR gave me for salaries more carefully:\n1. 10000z/ -> 10000\n2. 5000%」 -> 5000\n3. 5000元） -> 5000\n4. 10000元。-> 10000\n5. 5000之4 -> 5000\n6. 10000\n7. 1anoo之 -> 10000\n8. 100002 -> 10000\n9. 10000之1 -> 10000\n10. 1oc00z -> 10000\n11. Jan0o礼 -> 10000\n12. 10000\n13. 0000 -> probably 10000\n14. 15000之 -> 15000\n\nIf #12 is 10000 (not 0000) and #13 is 10000:\n10000*11 + 5000*3 + 15000 = 110000+15000+15000 = 140,000. Too high.\n\nIf #13 is 5000:\n10000*11 + 5000*4 + 15000 = 110000+20000+15000 = 145,000. Too high.\n\nIf #12 is 0000 (actually 0):\n10000*10 + 5000*3 + 0 + 15000 = 100000+15000+15000 = 130,000. Doesn't match.\n\nHmm, 15000*1 + 10000*11 + 5000*2 = 15000+110000+10000 = 135,000. Yes!\n\nSo: 1 person at 15000, 11 people at 10000, 2 people at 5000. But that's only 14 entries. The description says 17 people.\n\nActually wait, maybe I'm missing some rows. Let me re-read the output.\n\nActually this is getting complex with the garbled OCR. Let me just create the best possible version and present it to the user, noting that some characters may be misrecognized and ask them to verify.\n\nActually, let me try one more time with the OCR, using a different approach. Maybe I can extract the image portions separately.\n\nOr better yet, let me just proceed with what I have and create a clean CSV file. The user can then verify and correct.\n\nLet me try another approach - let me try the OCR again but with a prompt to get more structured output.\n\nActually, I think I should just produce the best result I can at this point and present it to the user. Many names and numbers will have OCR errors, but the core structure is there.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"好多了！这次识别效果提升不少。让我